# Risk surfaces: how much human and agent review attention a change to a path deserves.
# Read from the BASE branch by the pre-push review (skills-internal cross-model-review), so a PR
# cannot lower the tier of its own files. Format: `<tier> <glob>`, last match wins; a glob with no
# `/` matches at any depth. Defaults already cover path words like transaction, replication,
# storage, schema, migration, rocksdb, lmdb (critical) and auth, security, crypto (sensitive).
#
# critical  — correctness or durability of stored data, replication, wire/at-rest encodings
# sensitive — authentication, authorization, secrets
# hot       — request/read/write hot paths where a regression is a performance incident
# ordinary  — overrides a default

